 ## Overview
-Face Culling is a mesh generation optimization that reduces the number of vertices and triangles sent to the GPU by skipping the rendering of voxel faces that are adjacent to existing neighboring voxels [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of naively rendering all 6 faces of every cube, including those hidden by neighbors. It is distinguished from its siblings by performing a direct neighbor lookup for each face during mesh creation, rather than using bitwise bulk operations [S2, unofficial] or complex visibility masks [S3397-face-coverage-mask-culling.md].
+Face Culling is a mesh generation optimization that reduces the number of vertices and triangles sent to the GPU by skipping the rendering of voxel faces that are adjacent to existing neighboring voxels [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of naively rendering all six faces of every cube, including those hidden by neighbors, which results in excessive draw calls and vertex processing overhead [S1, unofficial]. Unlike [Block Visibility Culling](5334-block-visibility-visibility-culling.md) which operates at a higher level, Face Culling operates at the individual face level within a block, ensuring that only exposed surfaces contribute to the final mesh [S1, unofficial].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:** A set of occupied voxel positions (typically stored in a hash set or grid) and a list of voxels to process.
-**Outputs:** A vertex buffer containing only the visible faces of the voxel mesh.
+The method determines the visibility of each of the six faces of a voxel block by checking the occupancy state of its immediate neighbors in the 3D grid. A face is considered visible if the adjacent voxel in the direction of the face's normal is empty (air/void). If a neighbor exists and is opaque, the shared face is internal and is culled [Parent].
 
-**Data Structures:**
-The method relies on a representation of voxel occupancy. In the primary implementation, this is a boolean grid or a hash set of occupied positions [S1, unofficial].
-The `Cube` struct contains:
-- `std::vector<Face> faces` (size 6)
-- `glm::ivec3 cubeCenter`
-- `glm::ivec3 gridPos`
-- `int neighbors`
